=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play users/debian13 ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the User Management screen proposed for$
# slice 5, drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (users.Admin.Check, users.ReadElevation, sudoers.Read,$
# PolicyOf, Invoker, ssh.ReadPAM), each grant the real$
# sudoers.PlanFor on the real plan/apply engine. Creating a user$
# and the keys are the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build.$
# Nothing on this machine changes: every command and file is the$
# fake's.$
$
# Info: users/debian13$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. As the VM: george, uid$
# 1000, no password (!), in sudo and adm, two keys, NOPASSWD by$
# cloud-init's 90-cloud-init-users; alice, uid 1001, a password,$
# in sudo, no key. hardn runs through george's sudo.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
# alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           group sudo$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 2$
$
# Create User ##################################################$
$
   1. Username [0 or q]: carol$
$
   2. Grant sudo privilege? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
   3. Require sudo password? [y/N, 0 or q]: n$
$
   4. Add SSH key? [y/N, 0 or q]: n$
$
# Warning$
# Without a key carol can't log in: there's no password.$
$
# User Configuration -------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             None$
$
   -  Create user carol$
      /etc/passwd$
      -absent$
      +no password, key login$
      $ useradd --create-home --shell /bin/bash carol$
$
   -  Let carol use sudo$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-grant-carol$
      @@ -0,0 +1,2 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn$
      +carol ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL$
$
  No actual changes were made to your system.$
$
# User Management ##############################################$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
$
# george -------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Sudo                 Enabled, No password$
   -  Granted by           /etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users$
   -  SSH Keys             2 keys$
   -  Password             None$
$
# alice --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Sudo                 Enabled$
   -  Granted by           group sudo$
  [ ] SSH Keys             None$
   -  Password             Set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Manage User          Configure sudo, SSH keys$
   2) Create User          Configure a new user$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

